WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.120
Welcome back to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 494 from May 31st, 2026.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.960
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's get into what's moving in the Tesla world today.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:20.640
Looking back at 11 episodes from 2026-05-25 to 2026-05-31,

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:27.100
the stories that mattered what we learned and what to watch next. Tesla filed self-certification

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:34.040
for its Robotaxi software as SAE Level 4 in Texas. The filing secures commercial driverless

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:40.280
authorization under state rules in permitted zones. This step allows paid Robotaxi service

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:47.320
to begin once vehicles are deployed. Reports also note contracting fleet numbers in Austin, Dallas,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:54.240
and Houston. The move advances the regulatory path for unsupervised operation. It remains the

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.160
primary gating item for the CyberCab program after the Wii Robot unveiling.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.000
Next, we will watch for the first revenue generating trip under the new permit.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.280
Now shifting from the regulatory green light to the software that will run on those vehicles.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:16.120
FSD version 14.3.3 reduces driver monitoring chimes during routine drives.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:23.660
Owners report fewer interventions when adjusting music or navigation. A 130-mile mixed root test

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:28.360
on turnpikes, backroads, and small town streets required no driver takeover.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.580
Scenic drive positioning and GROC travel guide features rolled out for longer trips.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.940
The update refines attention monitoring thresholds in the latest branch.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:43.380
This shows incremental gains in handling edge cases that earlier versions flagged.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.900
While the supervised system improves, a separate long distance test is now pushing the same software

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:57.540
across borders. The driver who set the US coast to coast FSD supervised record has started a similar run

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:03.180
across Canada. The journey tests varying provincial roads, signage, and weather conditions.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.780
It also checks performance on routes with fewer mapped updates than major US corridors.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:14.080
Success would extend the documented range of supervised long distance travel.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.700
Completion time and any interventions required will be the next data point.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:26.020
As FSD expands geographically, hardware reliability in dirty conditions becomes a practical limit.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:32.960
Tesla filed a patent for a compact lens cleaning system with an integrated wiper blade and fluid

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:39.080
reservoir. The design includes automatic debris detection for autopilot and FSD cameras.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:44.320
It avoids large washer nozzles or external hardware that would add weight and complexity.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.860
The system triggers cleaning without driver input when build-up is detected.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.940
Clear vision remains essential in dirty or wet conditions for the supervised fleet.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.840
The next step is whether the patent appears in production vehicles later this year.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.620
Camera improvements matter for today's fleet, but production hardware programs are also moving.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:11.840
The $59,990 all-wheel drive Cybertruck variant is approaching customer handovers.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.460
The dual motor trim went on sale months ago and keeps the structural battery pack.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:22.480
Deliveries would mark the first expansion beyond the initial trim motor configuration.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.860
Production capacity at Giga Texas continues to set the pace for this program.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.820
While Cybertruck ramps, Tesla's halo vehicle plans are also advancing at the same Texas site.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.380
Executives confirm the second-generation roadster will be built at Giga Factory Texas.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:45.320
Planning for the production layout has begun, the first concrete statement on the car in nine years.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:51.500
No launch date has been set. The decision keeps the halo vehicle inside Tesla's Texas operations.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.980
Observers will watch for any updates on battery or motor specifications tied to the Texas site.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:03.740
Texas is also the site of another delayed high-profile program facing supply issues.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.680
The Optimus Humanoid Robot program has encountered a manufacturing constraint.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:14.320
The snag arrives as Giga Texas prepares dedicated assembly space for the project.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.760
Current plans still target initial volume production in 2027.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.160
The delay could compress the testing window before wider deployment.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.880
Observers will watch for updates on actuator or sensor supply chains in the coming quarters.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.260
This is the first public signal of a production bottleneck since dedicated factory construction began.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.340
Factory constraints are also surfacing on current vehicles.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:50.620
Tesla issued service bulletins SB 26-31-003 and SB 25-31-005 for front suspension noises

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.960
on refreshed model-wide vehicles.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.960
The documents formalize a repair process for persistent creaking on the Juniper platform.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.140
This addresses a known build quality complaint on the updated model.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.680
Owners should check service appointment availability once the bulletins are pushed.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.560
Rivian confirmed the R2 will open orders, offer demo drives, and begin deliveries on June 9.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:20.540
The vehicle is positioned directly against the model Y in the mid-size electric SUV segment.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:26.000
Quality notes on today's best-seller lead into broader questions about next year positioning.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:31.580
Tesla highlighted that owners can let FSD supervise to handle scenic road trips,

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.560
so passengers focus on the landscape.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.440
The message positions the supervised system as a practical tool for longer leisure drives.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.460
It comes as Tesla continues to expand FSD availability in new markets.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:50.020
GROC was positioned as an in-car travel guide for geological features and local history.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.880
Owners can say, hey GROC, to ask about nearby points of interest while traveling.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.800
The feature turns the voice assistant into a real-time companion for exploration.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:04.960
Estonia approved Tesla's full self-driving supervised software following

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.920
clearances in the Netherlands and Lithuania. The decision adds another European market where owners

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:16.740
can activate the supervised system. Regulators reviewed Tesla's safety data package before

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:22.620
granting access. One challenge worth discussing is the production bottleneck now facing Optimus,

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.320
just as dedicated space comes online at Giga Texas.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:32.880
The timeline for scaling still targets 2027 volume, yet the constraint arrives at a critical

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.500
preparation stage. This compresses the window for testing and refinement before wider deployment

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:44.700
begins. Supply chain details on actuators and sensors will determine whether the target holds.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:50.620
Tesla's top engineer confirmed he considers a trimotor Model 3 regularly,

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:57.740
but has chosen not to prioritize it. Development resources remain focused on other programs instead.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:04.280
The current Model 3 performance stays the top trim for now. Production capacity and software

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:09.740
priorities have taken precedence over adding another plaid variant. The underlying engineering

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:15.760
question here is how Tesla sequences limited resources across overlapping vehicle and robot programs.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:22.140
Each program shares the same Texas factory footprint and the same structural battery and compute

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:28.020
investments. When one area encounters a supply or assembly limit, the others feel the ripple

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:33.220
through shared capacity planning. Listeners can track whether actuator or sensor update

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:38.400
surface first for Optimus or whether cyber truck volume absorbs the near-term focus.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:45.340
Tomorrow, we will be watching for the first Revenue Robotaxi trip under the new Texas Level 4

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:52.520
filing and any early V14.3.3 rollout metrics. That's your Tesla news for today.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:08:04.680
TSLA closed at $435.79 down $6.31, 1.4%. If you found this useful, a rating or review on Apple

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:11.280
podcasts or Spotify really helps new listeners find the show. You can also find us on X at Tesla's

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:15.860
short time. I'm Patrick and Vancouver. Thanks for listening and I'll see you tomorrow.

